<title>AUSTRIA: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>AUSTRIA GOVERNMENT LIST (970118)</p>
<p>***********************************************************</p>
<p>* 18 Jan 97 - Franz Vranitzky resigned as Chancellor and  *</p>
<p>*		 was replaced by Viktor Klima. The finance   *</p>
<p>*		 portfolio is temporarily vacant.		*</p>
<p>***********************************************************</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>President (Sworn in 8 July 1992</p>
<p>    for 6-year term)............................Thomas KLESTIL</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>TWO-PARTY COALITION GOVERNMENT:</p>
<p>(Sworn in 12 Mar 96)</p>
<p> Chancellor................................Viktor KLIMA (SPOe)</p>
<p> Vice-Chancellor.....................Wolfgang SCHUESSEL (OeVP)</p>
<p>(Also Foreign Minister)</p>
<p>				- - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Agriculture &amp; Forestry................Wilhelm MOLTERER (OeVP)</p>
<p> Defence..............................Werner FASSLABEND (OeVP)</p>
<p> Economics...........................Johann FARNLEITNER (OeVP)</p>
<p> Education &amp; Culture...................Elisabeth GEHRER (OeVP)</p>
<p> Environment.........................Martin BARTENSTEIN (OeVP)</p>
<p> Finance......................................................</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs...........................See Vice-Chancellor</p>
<p> Health.................................Christa KRAMMER (SPOe)</p>
<p> Interior..................................Caspar EINEM (SPOe)</p>
<p> Labour &amp; Social Affairs.....................Franz HUMS (SPOe)</p>
<p> Justice.......................Nikolaus MICHALEK (Independent)</p>
<p> Science, Research &amp; Art................Rudolf SCHOLTEN (SPOe)</p>
<p> Women's Issues............................Helga KONRAD (SPOe)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - -</p>
<p>SECRETARIES OF STATE:</p>
<p> Foreign Ministry................Benita FERRERO-WALDNER (OeVP)</p>
<p> Public Works............................Karl SCHLOEGEL (SPOe)</p>
<p>				- - - - - -</p>
<p>PARTY AFFILIATIONS:</p>
<p>SPOe -- Social Democratic Party</p>
<p>OeVP -- People's Party</p>
<p>			     - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank President........................Klaus LIEBSCHER</p>
<p>(National Bank of Austria)</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>	     government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>	     Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>	     7968.</p>
<p>			 (End Government List)</p>
</text>
